{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And yet for your lives I will demand your blood.</b> Even though I will not demand the blood of other living creatures from your hand, nevertheless I will demand your blood for the sake of your lives, which are more precious to Me than the lives of all other living creatures. And this demand will come about in alternating circumstances: if the person merits, then 'from the hand of every beast I will demand it, and from the hand of man' — to save him." "<b>From the hand of every man's brother I will demand the life of the man.</b> If he does not merit this — that I would deliver him — and his fellow kills him, I will demand the life of the slain from the hand of his brother who killed him, to exact punishment from him, but not from the hand of the beast."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:30.187873109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}